**Carl Jung is a PASS as an Emerging Entity Gap — 34/100 — but the packet is written to steer the pipeline toward the one lane that is actually winnable.** Packet saved to `docs/content-analysis/entity-gaps/Carl-Jung.md`.

What the audit found:

- **The exact-name SERP is a fortress.** `Carl Jung`, `Carl Jung biography`, and every fact query (`wife`, `Red Book`) are owned by his personal Wikipedia page, Britannica, Biography.com, Psychology Today, official Jung institutes, and university presses. The −20 penalty (Wikipedia + multiple authoritative biographies) applies in full. No general-biography page 9takes could write would deserve to outrank those, so the entity-gap play is illusory.
- **Demand is huge but saturated-evergreen, not emerging.** The nearest catalyst is shadow work's continued 2026 mainstreaming — it sustains demand but opens no window. Local GSC shows effectively zero Jung queries (expected; no page exists).
- **One genuinely weak SERP exists:** `carl jung enneagram type` / `personality type` is held by personality-database, Boo, Medium posts, and hobbyist typology blogs. That long-tail — plus internal-hub value linking the Enneagram corpus to the people corpus — is the backlog's actual "psychology-hub-cluster" rationale for this page, and it survives this audit even though the entity-gap model fails.

Context worth knowing: `carl-jung` is the backlog's current in-progress item (started this morning), so the packet's Content Requirements section is written for that pipeline run: title on the contested-type thesis (never "biography"), present his type as argued 5w4-vs-9w1 rather than declared, treat hub interlinking as the main strategic value, and judge the page by long-tail and linking value — never exact-name metrics. Claims-to-avoid flags the big traps: Jung is *not* in the Enneagram's actual lineage (Ichazo/Naranjo), he's one of the most fake-quoted people online so every quote needs a primary-source trace, and the Nazi-era controversy needs careful named sourcing or omission.

Source depth itself is a non-issue (15/15): autobiography, the Red Book, the Freud–Jung letters, the filmed 1959 BBC *Face to Face* interview, and the Bair and McLynn biographies.

Sources: [Wikipedia: Carl Jung](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carl_Jung), [Britannica](https://www.britannica.com/biography/Carl-Jung), [Biography.com](https://www.biography.com/scientists/carl-jung), [Psychology Today](https://www.psychologytoday.com/us/blog/hide-and-seek/202310/the-life-of-carl-jung), [The SAP](https://www.thesap.org.uk/articles-on-jungian-psychology-2/carl-gustav-jung/), [jung.org](https://jung.org/pages/who-is-carl-jung), [Emma Jung — Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emma_Jung), [National Geographic](https://www.nationalgeographic.com/history/article/carl-jung-emma-jung-jungian-archetypes), [Princeton UP on Emma Jung](https://press.princeton.edu/ideas/emma-jungs-years-of-self-liberation), [The Red Book — Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Red_Book_(Jung)), [Philemon Foundation](https://philemonfoundation.org/works/red-book/), [Personality Junkie on Jung's Enneagram](https://personalityjunkie.com/08/enneagram-4-5-9-jung-personality-type/), [Boo profile](https://boo.world/database/profile/30001/carl-jung-personality-type), [Shadow work in 2026](https://lifecoachingtoday.com/shadow-work-in-2026/)
